            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-ventura/plat-svc/files/ventura-fan-status-monitor",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there some way we can do this feature without implementing it in shell?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-ventura/plat-svc/files/ventura-fan-status-monitor",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Hsu",
                        "email": "jason-hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "QuantaJasonHsu"
                    },
                    "message": "This method is based on Minerva, or do you have any suggestions for how to implement this feature? Thank you."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-ventura/plat-svc/files/ventura-fan-status-monitor",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know enough about how to map sensor health to LEDs but I believe there is some support in phosphor-led-manager for it, because IBM does this kind of thing on their system.  If there isn't support already, we should probably create a longer-term development item to be able to support it rather than doing it as shell scripts.\n\nI cleaned up the script a little bit to reduce the super-long lines and make it easier to review.  Any time I see a shell script with lines that wrap 3 times my eyes glaze over.  :D :D"
                }
            ],
